VibeOS kernel for the Xiaomi Pad 5 (nabu)
=========================================

This branch is Kumar-Jy's nabu kernel with a few VibeOS commits on top.

Base
----
  https://github.com/Kumar-Jy/linux, branch nabu/7.3.y,
  commit 97375316e2600223cbed12edc43e8d375fd22ab7 (their release v7.3.6-0).

Their commits are kept exactly as they are. All the Xiaomi Pad 5 work in
this tree (display at 120 Hz, NT36523 touch and pen, CS35L41 speakers,
Iris video, the SMB5 charger and IDTP9418 pen charger, SLPI sensors,
suspend, keyboard and hall sensor) is Kumar-Jy's, building on the
postmarketOS sm8150 kernel and on mainline Linux. Thank you.

What VibeOS adds
----------------
  arch/arm64/configs/vibeos-nabu.config
      Merged over their nabu_defconfig (then olddefconfig). Kernel
      release 7.3.6-nabu, no DWARF, the GENI SPI bus built in so touch
      works from the initramfs, the PM8XXX RTC built in, and the same
      general and USB peripheral options as the other VibeOS devices.

Build
-----
  make O=<out> ARCH=arm64 CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-linux-gnu- nabu_defconfig
  scripts/kconfig/merge_config.sh -m -O <out> <out>/.config arch/arm64/configs/vibeos-nabu.config
  make O=<out> ARCH=arm64 CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-linux-gnu- olddefconfig
  make O=<out> ARCH=arm64 CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-linux-gnu- LOCALVERSION= Image.gz modules dtbs

The boot image is header v0 (page 4096) with Image.gz followed by
arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-nabu.dtb, and the slot's dtbo
partition erased.
